Z||000000||yunvme||01-07-2001||06:40 PM||||<BR>ive got a 2m4 and i was wondering what people have fit behind the seats as far as box size and sub? i can have the seat all the way up so i got some room atleast. any body got ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||qwikgta||01-07-2001||06:57 PM||||Since I don't care  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> about pass comfort I am going to make a box for behind the pass seat.  Im going to put one 12" in the box.  Another idea may be to use the foot well on the pass side too.  This would allow the seat to go all the way to the back and the pass would lose some foot room but again I don't care  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> about their comfort.  Hope it helps<P><P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top||||reg||7
Z||000002||stimpy||01-07-2001||11:10 PM||||Hey new folks! As far as info on beat in  Fiero goes, there is a lot of info here in the forum.  Do a search on subwoofers and you'll have hours of entertaining reading.  As far as woofers behind the seats, the most effective install I've seen has been fierosound's, which does ivlve a small amount of cutting into the rear firewall and no small amount of fabrication skill.  Personally, it wouldn't work for me.  Besides my phobia of cutting, I'm very tall and must drive with my seat all the way back. The passnger seat being moved up would obscure my vision to cross traffic. <BR>I went with the footwell method. Here is a pic of the enclosure I made. (And I am not an exceptionally handy guy)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=34099626&Sequence=5&res=high"> <BR>If you look closely you will see the the sealed enclosure does not take up more room then the pedals do on the drivers side, so legroom really isn't dramatically affected. A 10" fits nicely, possibly a 12 if it was angled correctly. My 10" works fine for me though.  ||||reg||1
